# Make a Dragonkin and photograph the character sheet.
#
# This exists for one assertion: a Dragonkin must have Mantis Leap. The feat is
# on the species template (lib/subraces.irh:731) and for years no player ever
# received it, because Character::HasFeat did not read the template. See inc-2a0.
#
# Race, subrace, class and alignment use @choose to select by name, so a
# list added to lib/ cannot change those choices. See src/Wposix.cpp.
# Run with a fixed seed: attribute rolls change the offered feats, and the
# attribute set and feat picks stay positional because sets have no names
# and feats depend on the rolls. Start-menu, question and movement keys
# stay counted for the reasons below.
# Header said every choice was a menu letter; corrected 2026-09-12.
# tools/check_race_feats.sh supplies the seed.

@expect "Initial Choices"
a       # Create a New Character: start menu is not a screen @choose reads.
@expect "Alter the character generation options?"
n       # Alter the character generation options? No: a yes/no question.
@expect "Explore Mode. Continue?"
y       # Continue in Explore Mode? Yes: a yes/no question.
@choose "Lizardfolk"
@choose "Dragonkin"
@choose "Barbarian"
@expect "Which of the five attribute sets"
a       # First attribute set: the five offered sets have no names.
@choose "Neutral"
@expect "Choose a feat"
a       # First feat: offered feats depend on the attribute rolls.
@expect "Choose a feat"
a       # Second feat: offered feats depend on the attribute rolls.

# Skill Manager. Three RIGHTs per skill spends everything available
# without needing to know how many ranks this character has.
@expect "Skill Manager"
# RIGHT/DOWN allocate ranks and move between skills, not named choices.
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Finish and keep the ranks: ENTER is a control, y answers yes/no.

@expect "Your personality archetype"
y       # No match: the sixteen personality entries use [a] through [p].

# RIGHT/DOWN move the personality selection to The Manipulative Plotter.
# Personality affects only the sheet banner, so its selection is not pinned.

RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN RIGHT*3 DOWN
ENTER y # Accept the selected archetype, then dismiss the entry description.

# In the dungeon now. The sheet is two screens; the feats block is on the
# second, so both are dumped and the check greps across them.
@expect "Things in View"
d
@dump:sheet1
@expect "[ESC] Return to Game"
DOWN*20
@dump:sheet2
ESC
@quit
